Those numbers should stay near the burdens named in the same passage: foundation problems, septic problems, roofing problems, payoff goals, and continuous work. A useful reconstruction is $\text{rental ownership}
=
\text{asset base}
+
\text{cash flow}
-
\text{repairs}
-
\text{debt service}
-
\text{management burden}.$ This is the book’s needed balance. Real estate can use leverage, time, and residual asset value, but the operator still has to survive the costs that arrive between purchase and payoff.

