Let $P_{\mathrm{contract}}$ be the contract price and $P_{\mathrm{end}}$ the end-buyer price. The gross spread is $S_{\mathrm{gross}}
=
P_{\mathrm{end}}-P_{\mathrm{contract}},$ with the required condition $P_{\mathrm{end}}>P_{\mathrm{contract}}.$ This is the wholesaler’s version of below-value control. The transcript gives no land numbers, so the book should not invent any. The mechanism is the spread.

