p.src:
Lecture 158 also gives a real-estate-specific media case. The marketing team says a class may reach $10$ people, while social media can reach hundreds of thousands or millions. In the podcast room, the aspiration is sharpened: instead of talking to $10$ people, talk to $10$ million. If $A_{\mathrm{room}}$ is the live-room audience and $A_{\mathrm{social}}$ is the online audience, then $M_{\mathrm{reach}}
=
\frac{A_{\mathrm{social}}}{A_{\mathrm{room}}}.$ For example, $\frac{100{,}000}{10}=10{,}000.$ As elsewhere in the book, reach is not revenue. But in this brokerage context, reach enlarges the surface for agents, recruits, relationships, and deals.

