The dynamic-book implication is narrow and important. Real estate should not be presented only as an asset class or an accessible industry. Lecture 158 shows it as a stack: $\text{below-value control}
+
\text{leverage}
+
\text{time}
+
\text{platform}
+
\text{media}
+
\text{lead process}.$ That stack is the new evidence. It belongs beside the arena-selection material, with cross-links to sales, media leverage, operations, and capital judgment.

